#set page(
    "us-letter",
    margin: 1cm
)
#show title: set align(center)
#set document(
    title: [
        Megadungeon of the Mad Archmage Gary-Stu, Level 1: Entry
    ]
)
#set text(
    font: "Helvetica Neue",
    weight: "light",
    size: 8pt
)
#set par(
    leading: 0.3em
)
#set heading(numbering: "1.")
#title()
#grid(
    columns: (69%, 2%, 28%),
    grid.cell(
        image(
            "/Users/adam/git/svgmapper/examples/svg/entry.svg",
             width: 100%
        )
    ),
    grid.cell([]),
    grid.cell(
        [
                *Wandering Monsters*\
                check every 2 turns, 1 in 8 chance.
                + Giant Toad (AC 14; HP 15; Bite +3 1d6+swallow)
                + 2 human bandits (AC 13 [leather + shield]; HP 9, 3; Longsword +1 1d8+1)
                + Rat swarm (AC 13; HP 8; Bite + 0 1d2 + disease)
                + Giant Centipede (AC 12; HP 4; Bite + 0 1d4 + poison)
                + Skeleton Warrior (AC 15, HP 6; Scimitar + 1 1d6+1)
                + Ghostly moaning
                + Sewage stench
                + Discarded, bloody bandages and empty potion flask

                *Legend*
                - *C* Concealed Door
                - *X* Pit in floor

                *Appendix A*
                Any time a wandering monster check indicates an encounter, on any level, roll d100.
                If the number rolled is less than or equal to the dungeon level, instead of rolling on the level-specific table, the party meets Gary-Stu

                Gary-Stu is a portly man with a gray ponytail and beard, wearing glasses and a garish Hawaiian shirt, smoking a cigar of remarkable vileness.
        ]
    )
)
*Room Key*
+ *Guard Post*: 2 goblin guards (AC 14 [scale mail]; HP 5,2; Morningstar +2 1d6).  Each has 8 sp, 12cp.
+ *Orc and Pie*: Snouty the orc (AC 16 [chain mail and shield]); HP 8; Falchion +4 (2d4 +4).  Tasty pie (cherry).
+ *Pit Trap*: Covered 30' pit in center of floor, DC 19 to not fall in, DC 5 to detect if anyone looks for it.  3d6 falling damage to room 19 of Level 2, Caves.
+ *Tripwire and spears*: tripwire 18" off floor, DC 12 to spot if anyone asks.  If triggered, 2 spears +6, 1d8 each.
+ *Barracks*: 11 bunks, 8 goblins.  If asleep, will take 2 rounds to wake up, 3 more rounds to get dressed and armored.  HP 7, 3, 4, 2, 7, 7, 3, 4.
+ *Feast Hall*: 6 goblins playing craps.  233 sp, a Lucky Amulet (+1 to hit), and 33cp in the pot.  HP 4, 2, 9, 9, 5, 3.
+ *Goblins' Kitchen*: Kobold _chef de cuisine_ (AC 13; HP 4; Cleaver +0, 1d6-1).  3 halfling line cooks (speak only Spanish) (AC 18; HP 3, 2, 3; Knife +0, 1d4).
+ *Goblins' Storeroom*: 6 barrels of beer (20gp/200lb), bunch of flour/salt pork/coffee.  Well and spiral stairs to wine cellar.
+ *Throne Room*: Hobgoblin Chieftain Grak (AC 15 [chain mail]; HP 13; Greataxe +5 (1d12+2) and 2 goblin guards (HP 6,2).  Grak has 125 gp gem, 38 gp.
+ *Chief's Quarters*: big waterbed, silk sheets, incense.  Total value 150gp, but bulky.  1 female goblin, asleep (HP 2).  Tapestry conceals door.
+ *Harem*: 3 noncombatant female goblins, 1 orc crone (AC 12; HP 6; club +3 1d6+1). 225 gp in assorted jewelry, cosmetics, etc.
+ *Vizier's Quarters*: Joey Granitethighs, Dwarf (AC 18 [plate]; HP 11; Waraxe +4 (1d8+1)). Gold Chain Of Office worth 55 gp, 22 gp, 18 sp.
+ *Lieutenant's Quarters*: Urgh the Hobgoblin.  (AC 15 [scale mail + shield], HP 13, Longsword +3, 1d8+2).  11 gp.
+ *Treasure Room*: Golden idol of Grummush worth 270 gp, 113 gp, 19 pp, 344 sp, 12 gems 10-60 gp each. Cask of cognac worth 200 gp (40 lbs).
+ *Bath*: Unguents and incenses worth 15 gp.
+ *Ramp to Surface*: roll logs, barrels, etc. down to storeroom.
+ *Guard Post*: 2 goblin guards (HP 5, 7).
+ *Corwyn's Room*: Corwyn, Fighter 2: (AC 19 [plate + shield]; HP 24; longsword +4 1d8+2). 25 gp, potion of cure light wounds.
+ *Grand Staircase*: Up to surface, down to level 8.
+ *Jenna's Room*: Jenna, MU 2. (AC 11; HP 13; dagger +1, 1d4). _Sleep_, _Charm Person_. Spellbook with those spells, 38 gp.
+ *Dojo*: Master Chu (AC 14; HP 20; 2 fists/feet +2, 1d6+3).  No treasure.
+ *Mess Hall*: 1 monk sweeping (AC 12; HP 14; punch +1, 1d6).  No treasure.
+ *Kitchen*: Kobold _chef de cuisine_, 3 halfling line cooks (see room 7).
+ *Monks' Cells*: All empty; contain only pallet, bowl, spoon.
+ *Toilets*: Actual flushing toilets.  This is a classy dungeon.
+ *Entry Hall*: 3 human monks (AC 12; HP 10, 12, 9; punch +1, 1d6).  No treasure.
+ *Monks' Storeroom*: Flour, dried vegetables, potatoes, turnips, etc.  Monks are vegetarian.
+ *Koan Hall*: Master Wu (AC 16; HP 24; 2 fists/feet +2, 1d8+3).  No treasure.
+ *Archery Range*: 2 monks (AC 12; HP 5,5; light crossbow +1, 1d6).  No treasure.
+ *Sluice*: clean, fast-flowing water.